n the story when  she suddenly appeared on the ship  inviting herself to join the crew in  retrospect however i think it makes a  lot of sense that luffy saved and  accepted robin on his ship because as we  learned from rayleigh during the time  skip luffy has the ability to sense a  person's true intentions so while luffy  was already aware of robin's true nature  it took us a whole lot more to truly  understand robin's character and  motivations and i dare say that this  process led to some of the best arcs in  the story the timing and pace that oda  used to place nico robin in the story  was simply amazing when looking at the  story up until the time skip having a  mysterious and complex antagonist with a  cool and dark vibe turn into an ally and  then slowly revealing the history and  impact of that character everything  about this character introduced a new  level of complexity and heaviness to the  story that didn't really exist up to  that point  robin's past the genocide of her people  her life-long run from the grasp of the  world government and the loneliness and  heartbreak she experienced really  hammered in what one piece was going to  be about in the long run with robin we  were introduced to the poneglyphs and  with them to the mystery of the ancient  kingdom its weapons and the source of  injustice in the world with the  introduction of the cp9 we were shown  the cruelty and ruthlessness with which  the world government operated and how  corrupt and unjust the entire system  truly was  with robin one piece changed its nature  and scale of complexity it went from a  young boy trying to find the ultimate  treasure in the world of pirates  together with his friends to a political  and complex story about healing the  world and breaking the unjust and cruel  system under which the world is  suffering robin as a character is  constructed in a way that mirrors  everything that is wrong with the  current system when she joins the crew  her greatest weaknesses are her deep  lack of trust in anyone but herself a  great lack of self-confidence and  self-worth and a strong sense of  loneliness and isolation  all these things can easily be tracked  back to her past while she had already  been tormented by her uncle and his wife  and feared by the other children for her  devil fruit powers it took the entire  cruelty of the world government to rob  young robin from all her positivity and  hope first her mother and everyone she  knew were murdered in front of her eyes  then they brainwashed the public into  believing that robin was the last  survivor of a group that was trying to  destroy the world by finding the ancient  weapons they robbed her of any chance of  refuge or care so robin had to grow up  on her own hiding and on the run  as a result robin has a clear moral  problem that her character needs to  solve her inability to trust and open up  to others keeps her from following the  path she actually wants to go to learn  and to live in peace while she's  actually a very kind-hearted and caring  person her tragic past has forced her to  put up a wall around herself that keeps  her from making any friends and since  she doesn't trust anyone she ends up  hurting those around her as well by  manipulating and using them for her own  interests when she's taken by the cp9  even though she already wants to protect  the crew her inability to share her  thoughts and feelings with others end up  hurting her friends the big challenge  for robin's character was therefore to  overcome this wall that she had built  around herself and once again allow  herself to open up and trust others  on the surface at first glance robin's  dream doesn't really seem to be  connected to this need her dream is to  learn the true history of the world and  uncover what was lost and hidden given  her heritage of o'hara and her passion  for archaeology this of course makes  sense and i hope you agree with me when  i say that robin's dream is a lot more  relevant to the actual plot than some of  the other straw hats compared to brook  or sanji for example whose dreams are  more personal robin's dream is directly  connected to opposing the strongest  political and military force on the  planet her dream goes hand in hand with  reaching raftel and making luffy the  pirate king i had a real click moment in  my head when i saw how perfectly that  dream fit in with her character but  going back to her moral problem robin  also has a second dream that is actually  on a more personal level robin wants to  find someone to protect and in that  sense she is already in the unique  position where she's aware of a moral  problem something that usually takes a  very impactful event to uncover in  robin's case though it simply shows us  how deep her vulnerability really goes  even though she knows that she wants to  love and trust people she has suffered  too much to overcome it herself both of  these dreams also go really well hand in  hand with the values that robin holds as  we keep learning over the course of the  story robin is a much more positive  person than she appears in the beginning  she actually strongly values trust  kindness and relationships in general  her twisted sense of humor seems to be a  result of these ideals and the harsh  reality she had to live in being a woman  of science similar to chopper she also  highly values knowledge and the way it  is used also as you know being the most  political amongst the crew robin clearly  values peace which is why we can see  robin at her happiest when she's reading  a book on board of the ship out at sea  most importantly though robin finally  learns to value life not only life of  others but especially her own which is  one of the greatest moral messages of  oda in the entire story i feel because  being able to love yourself for who you  are is probably the most important  factor in growing as a person and  finding happiness  based on these values and her past robin  is an incredibly intelligent and  knowledgeable character being at the  center of political interest she  probably has the most realistic and  complete view of the world in the crew  and having to survive all this time by  herself she has learned to play smart  and also dirty if necessary together  with her calm and collected manner and  her for me personally hilarious dark  humor i would say that she has developed  a really strong personality and since  she plays such an important role in the  story robin of course has also gathered  a number of powerful opponents that only  maybe luffy can come close to being on  the top wanted list of the world  government and all its organizations  robin has enemies all over the world  including the citizens  additionally pirates and other  organizations also crave her skills  putting her at danger anywhere she goes  to best illustrate how all of these  factors come together in the story let's  now take a look at robin's character arc  i think that it will not come as a big  surprise to you when i tell you that  robin's main character arc took place  over the course of two major arcs the  baroque work saga and the water 7 and  anna's lobby arc first being introduced  as an antagonist we got to know of robin  stark and mysterious side basically the  result of her tragic past her character  only begins to truly change though when  she's rescued by luffy from the tomb in  alabasta upon deciding to join the crew  since she has nowhere else to go robin  slowly starts to experience friendship  and kindness as she hasn't since she met  saul on o'hara she was slowly accepted  by the crew and even though she didn't  truly feel like a part of them she still  learned to appreciate this new and  positive environment she found herself  in so after simply being a normal part  of the crew for the entirety of the  skypia arc robin started to feel  connected to the crew a moral problem  and lack of self-confidence though led  her to leave the crew behind to protect  them from the influence of the world  government she wanted to shield the  straw hats from the greatest scheme of  things and keep them out of the world of  politics and save from any prosecution  by oda making anna's lobby into a major  developing arc for the entire crew  though he made the message to robin even  more powerful her friends would not only  stand behind her but overcome their  limits and become stronger just for her  sake they were prepared to take on the  biggest power in the world just for her  luffy did not simply put her above his  interests he made her part of them the  entirety of the innis lobby arc is  simply amazing how oda was able to bring  together so many different elements and  push the story in so many ways all by  creating robin the way she is  so when she sees how important she  actually is to others she is finally  able to overcome an inability to put  trust and hope into others and opens  herself up to the straw hats i think  that it's no surprise then that this  moment is one of the most impactful ones  in the entire story  at the same time robin is also able to  achieve one of her dreams and has  finally found someone she can protect  and care for she was truly able to  challenge her basic beliefs and in the  end managed to overcome her weaknesses  and break down her wall i can say with  confidence that robin's character arc up  until the time skip is one of my  favorite ones in fiction  so if you watched my video on chopper  you probably know what is coming now  because same as chopper i feel like  robin's character has a big problem  because in more than just one way her  character arc has already finished by  the time skip and i do not complain  about that as i just said i believe her  arc was simply incredible and greatly  set up by oda the problem is that i  don't see anything new happening with  robin  similar to chopper she has also lost her  mysterious and cool vibe and has now  become someone with a funny hat that  keeps in the background most of the time  and smiles a lot it sometimes literally  feels like oda has sucked all excitement  out of this amazing character and  especially in robin's case i feel that  that is such a waste because her  character is so complex and has so many  sides that there was more than one  option to keep robin relevant and  fascinating isn't her character  interesting enough to serve as more than  just a technical piece in reaching  raftel and learning the truth because  even though robin has changed the fact  that she's still one of the most  notoriously wanted people in the world  shouldn't have changed robin has so many  capabilities and yet never has played  any major role in any arc since the time  skip she is so well versed in the  political structures of the world and  was part of the underworld herself and  yet in dressrosa as well as in whole  cake island where the underworld and  political structures played such a big  role she didn't play any and apart from  that robin has one of the most amazing  devil fruits in the story she could  literally spy on anyone by creating eyes  anywhere she can create clones but only  uses them in very limited ways she could  maybe create additional muscles to power  up her physical strength but how in the  world does it fit her smart and witty  character that she decided to use her  fruit to make giant arms and legs that  aimlessly stomp around isn't that rather  something that a luffy or a frankie  would do with all the opportunities this  fruit has especially for her character  outside and inside of combat this power  could be used so much smarter even  though i think her character change was  handled amazingly i don't think that  overcoming her weaknesses and finding  friends necessarily had to mean turning  her into a playing character why not  keep her edge and sinister vibe for a  bit her smooth confident attractive and  dangerous personality is gone and she is  now easily overshadowed by strong  personalities like luffy zorro or even  usop now don't get me wrong as we have  established before robin still has to  play an important role in the story we  pretty much don't know what she was up  to with the revolutionaries during the  time skip and she might very well still  keep her secrets she will play a  decisive role in tumbling the world  government and maybe even in creating a  new and just world order but i still  wish that oda would have left some of  the fascination in her character and  gave her some new character arc in the  new world because robin is the  lightbringer the devil for the world  government and the light of the  revolution and i think both of these  roles deserve a little bit more  attention and development  and maybe a new leather jacket

